sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Alice as alice (rules:author)
  actor Bob as bob (rules:approve)
  participant SVC as VersionService (replica A)
  participant DB as PostgreSQL (rle_version, rle_rule_set)
  participant B as Replica B (compiled cache)

  Alice->>SVC: :request-publish v2, effectiveFrom, If-Match "4", Idempotency-Key
  SVC->>DB: type-check passes then UPDATE status=PENDING_APPROVAL, requested_by=alice WHERE status='DRAFT' AND lock_version=4
  SVC-->>Alice: 200, ETag "5", event rules.version.publish-requested.v1
  Alice->>SVC: :approve v2
  SVC-->>Alice: 403 SELF_APPROVAL_FORBIDDEN (approver equals requested_by, checked before any write)
  Bob->>SVC: :approve v2, If-Match "5", Idempotency-Key
  alt bob differs from requested_by, status PENDING_APPROVAL, lockVersion 5
    SVC->>DB: UPDATE status=PUBLISHED, approved_by=bob, lock_version=6 then cache_epoch+1 then event rules.version.published.v1 then COMMIT
    SVC->>DB: pg_notify('horus_rle_cache', tenant, rule set, epoch) after commit
    SVC-->>Bob: 200, ETag "6"
  else stale If-Match or already decided
    SVC-->>Bob: 409 VERSION_CONFLICT or 409 INVALID_STATE
  end
  alt LISTEN connection available
    DB-->>B: NOTIFY: evict entry within milliseconds
  else transaction-mode pooler or dropped listener
    B->>DB: epoch sweep every cache.epoch-check-interval (5 s): cache_epoch moved, evict
  end
  Note over DB,B: Evaluation picks the latest effective_from <= clock, so v2 applies at effectiveFrom without a wake-up. The scheduler retires v1 then and emits rules.version.retired.v1
